{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1116888-changelings-and-demons","id":1116888,"title":"Changelings and Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-16T10:24:12-07:00","id":1116888,"title":"Changelings and Demons","content":"How do changelings and demons interact in your games? In ours, Kithain are the remnants of the Holy Host, and Fallen and Kithain sense each other on sight. We had a &quot;thrall immunity&quot; in our last game, as far as changelings are concerned. I might keep that. Kinain would essentially be Nephilim from a Demon's point of view, wouldn't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T11:48:40-07:00","id":1116928,"title":"","content":"I have them be completely incompatible cosmologies, that get very confused if they ever have a long enough conversation to go through their histories. <br /> <br /> I do also have someone who's a Dreamer be a pretty potent Thrall, making conflicts over resources nasty. <br /> <br /> Plus I find the concept of an Earthbound in the Dreaming something I want to have show up in game at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T15:58:24-07:00","id":1116992,"title":"","content":"I tend to kinda agree with zenten. The Fae and Demons are incompatible in a way, meaning that their facts about existence tend to conflict. Devil's Due, basically Dark Ages Demon, had a some information on how it would match to DA:Fae, which I have since then used as a basic guideline.<br /> <br /> In DD it's basically said that the Demons do not remember creating the Fae nor that they even existence during the rebellion which immediately makes them stand out. Are they beings created by the Host after the rebellion or beings brought here from another world created by the divine or most worrisomely are they a creation of humanity through their collective Faith. The Fae see Demons as just another odd being that does not concern them that much since they have so little to give to the Fae, but the Fae do cheer the Demons when they make trouble for the church.<br /> <br /> Of thralldom, and possession, I again like to take the DD approach, even though it is written with DA: Fae in mind. According to it Firstborn and the Inanimae are unable to be bound in pacts and too alien to be possessed but Changelings on the other hand can be both. When taken in CtD terms, and Now C20, I ruled it to mean that only those Fae who had a human component to their soul, that is those that went through the changeling way ritual, are able to be thralls or be possessed by Demons mostly meaning that the Dark-kin and the Arcadian Sidhe, and the few other Fae who have not gone through the ritual, cannot become thralls or be possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T16:34:25-07:00","id":1117008,"title":"","content":"In my games, Changelings state overtly that Demons are just Christian themed Fae created by the Abrahamic religions belief system versus their Celtic origins.<br /> <br /> Demons...disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:00:17-07:00","id":1117102,"title":"","content":"Interesting. Demons with Torment 4 or above register as corrupt. This makes Kithain think &quot;Fomorian&quot; ... and then things get ugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T05:34:01-07:00","id":1117159,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Recaps and sluagh should also seem &quot;corrupt&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:50:07-07:00","id":1117417,"title":"","content":"Changeling would be much less interesting without either. I play both kith almost exclusively. Thanks for letting me know about the rules in Devil's Due We didn't get enough in C20, though I expected that, considering how much they had to cover already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T14:04:05-07:00","id":1117428,"title":"","content":"What I mean is while the Seelie might not generally like high Torment demons, I don't think most of the Kithain will assume Formorians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:25:41-07:00","id":1118701,"title":"","content":"We had quite a few moronic house rules in the last game I was in, too many of which favored DtF. That was one of the less stupid ones. I was waiting for Changeling 20th to come out so I could figure out something less broken. It might be interesting if a literally Earthbound Demon binds itself to a freehold as a Reliquary. Or even worse, the balefire itself. I can see gatherings of Fallen refugees in the Dreaming, since they can use trods in Apocalyptic form and the Dreaming (might) anchor them from Hell's spiritual gravity.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know what the &quot;beacon for hunters, Technocrats, and others who would do him harm&quot; is in Demon? What does &quot;befoul[ing] the environment&quot; refer to? The presence of an Earthbound Reliquary, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:57:36-07:00","id":1118759,"title":"","content":"Since Demons don't understand the Umbra (it came about after the rebellion), I don't think they could make a reliquary of a freehold. They just...wouldn't even notice it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T17:05:15-07:00","id":1118763,"title":"","content":"Freeholds have nothing to do with the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T12:54:19-07:00","id":1120452,"title":"","content":"Though they have everything to do with the Dreaming, which Demons probably cannot perceive considering that Changelings aren't even mentioned in any of the Demon books that I have read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-25-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:04:54-07:00","id":1120457,"title":"","content":"High Banality for an entire splat has been thrown out in C20, and rightly so. So even Vampires and Technocrats don't necessarily have a high Banality anymore; it would be really weird if Demons did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:48:22-07:00","id":1120831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1116888-changelings-and-demons?p=1120457#post1120457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Banality for an entire splat has been thrown out in C20, and rightly so. So even Vampires and Technocrats don't necessarily have a high Banality anymore; it would be really weird if Demons did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that; Technocrats still seem presented as having a rather high Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:10:18-07:00","id":1121014,"title":"","content":"C20 Technocrats can't serve as Dreamers, and C20 Demons' host bodies do have high Banality. Both of which I'm ignoring because it makes crossover difficult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T23:50:27-07:00","id":1214942,"title":"","content":"I like the Idea that the Tuatha could be related to the Children Lilith had with other Gods and Demons. And if Hsien are Fae long ago, then they are very close to Demons as they are both Heavenly agents. But hell Tuatha and Fomorians could have been started by Angels, and all the rest are their Progeny. Glamour eating seems like an evolution of Faith eating. Primordial Dark Age Fae is all about plucking potential from the Mists, that seems an aweful lot like Lore Carving Creation from the First Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T02:12:51-07:00","id":1214973,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to point out yet again the difference between &quot;arcadian Sidhe&quot; and &quot;Demon&quot; from an outside perspective isn't all that great. Fallen returns even match up very well when the Thallain and Dark Kin were released en masse. Fallen have a story of about being outcast from their fellow shining Ones for their actions. They even organize themselves into HOUSES...<br /> <br /> I'm just saying it looks odd that The Fallen match up rather well to Sidhe who've fallen to the corruption of the Formorians.. even Torment being a &quot;Gift' of the formorians is right there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T18:12:57-07:00","id":1227791,"title":"","content":"This is why when I want to play Demon, I actually play In Nomine. All of this was considered all ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T08:16:57-07:00","id":1228589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1116888-changelings-and-demons?p=1118763#post1118763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freeholds have nothing to do with the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true. As it was explained in Second Edition, the Dreaming cuts through various levels of the Umbra, even if it is technically its own thing. It's a strata that cuts through High and Middle Umbra, and in places touches upon the Dark Umbra. Maybe it was Dreams and Nightmares on the Storytellers Guide that explained it? I can't remember.<br /> <br /> Freeholds (at least, the fae part) are where the Dreaming seeps into/touches the Autumn World. So by extension, I just don't see demons interacting with freeholds, and definitely not the chimerical elements. They probably can't see chimerical reality anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}